# Trivy ignore — NARROW, dev-tooling only. Each CVE below is a HIGH in a transitive
# dependency of ESLint (dev/build tooling), NOT reachable in the production runtime.
#
# Why these are safe to ignore (and ONLY these):
#  - `npm why <pkg> --omit=dev` shows NO production dependency path — they are
#    pulled solely by eslint / @eslint/config-array, which are devDependencies of
#    the root project (e.g. cross-spawn ← eslint; minimatch ← @eslint/config-array).
#  - The production runtime entrypoint is `node dist/index.cjs` (an esbuild bundle
#    of prod externals: canvas, sharp, pdfkit, pg, @aws-sdk, resend, helmet). None
#    of these packages are on that path.
#  - Scope is exactly these CVE IDs. OS/base-image CVEs (e.g. libgnutls30,
#    libcap2) are NOT ignored — those are patched via `apt-get upgrade` in the
#    Dockerfile. No broad package/severity class is ignored.
#
# Revisit if any of these packages ever enters the production dependency tree.

# cross-spawn (← eslint) — regular-expression DoS
